    "reasoning": "q-36911: The gradient is (2x/(x^2+1),4(y-3)). Its components vanish exactly when x=0 and y=3. The worked solution mistakenly writes ln(x+1) in its y-derivative calculation; this transcription error does not change that derivative or the final answer. q-36970: The gradient equations are y(1+y)=0, x(1+2y)=0, and 3z^2=0. Thus y=0 or -1, and either case requires x=z=0. The source mistakenly refers to ∇f instead of ∇h and repeats j instead of k on the zero-vector side; its final points are correct. q-181683: The shaded region lies above y=-x-3 and below y=x+4. Both boundaries are solid, so both inequalities include equality. The points belong to the real coordinate plane R^2. All five field answers agree with their own captured worked solutions; no submitted grades were supplied.",
